{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 40, :comments ["<b>That you may remember and do all My commandments.</b> Our Rabbis of blessed memory expounded regarding the obligation of reading Shema morning and evening that one must pronounce the zayin of תזכרו distinctly. The reason for this is so that the word not become garbled for us and be understood as תשכרו with a shin, which is an expression of hiring, because one must not perform the commandments on condition of receiving reward. We may say further that this is in order to allude to the five books of the Torah, which are divided into seven, for this commandment is equivalent to the entire Torah. It is also possible to say regarding the distinct pronunciation of the zayin that it alludes to the great Sabbath, and the sense of the verse is to say: I command you this commandment of tekhelet that you perform it below, that you may remember above the quality that is within the quality of the All, which is the great Sabbath. And it says, ״and you shall do all My commandments,״ because all the commandments are included there; and this is clear."], :book :numbers, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 15, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:32:50.601041682Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}